+## NMOS node: the `mxl-nmos` crate
+
+The NMOS node is the shared crate `LeeO86/mxl-nmos` (a release tag in
+`backend/Cargo.toml`). `backend/src/nmos/glue.rs` maps flows to its resources and
+keeps the activation handler, which still restarts the whole flow.
+
+Follow-up (not done): the crate calls the activation handler for one sender or
+receiver at a time and never restarts anything itself. That makes the fix for
+"a connection change restarts the whole flow" possible: apply the new
+`mxl_domain_id` / `mxl_flow_id` to the one MXL block (for example by rebuilding
+only that block's elements) instead of stopping and starting the flow.
diff --git a/docs/CHANGELOG.md b/docs/CHANGELOG.md
index 2d45059..ecf9491 100644
--- a/docs/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/docs/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,26 @@
 
 All notable changes to the Strom GStreamer Flow Engine project.
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Changed
+- The NMOS node is now the shared crate [`mxl-nmos`](https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-nmos) 0.1.0. Strom keeps the glue: flows with MXL blocks become Devices, output blocks Source + Flow + Sender, input blocks Receivers, and an activation still restarts the flow. Ids, labels, settings, readiness wiring, shutdown and export/import are unchanged.
+- `/readyz` now also needs the Query API (`NMOS_QUERY_ADDRESS` / `NMOS_QUERY_PORT`, default registry address and port + 1) to list the node.
+- IS-04 `version` and IS-05 `activation_time` are TAI (`CLOCK_TAI`), no longer UTC; versions strictly increase and change on every activation. The host's kernel TAI offset must be set (37 s).
+- An IS-05 activation waits up to 30 s for the flow restart, then answers 500.
+- The Node `href` is the API base URL; Devices list the Connection API in `controls`; audio Sources carry `channels` (moved from the audio Flow, where IS-04 has no such field); bulk results carry `error` and `debug`.
+- After an activation, `/staged` keeps `auto` as staged; `/active` shows the resolved ids.
+- With `NMOS_DNS_SD=true` the node also browses `_nmos-register._tcp` (IS-04 v1.3) and advertises itself only while no registry is known, with `api_auth`.
+
+### Added
+- Scheduled IS-05 activations (absolute and relative, TAI); they answered 400 before.
+- CI job `nmos-amwa`: AMWA BCP-007-03-01 against Strom with an nmos-cpp registry (`scripts/nmos-amwa/`).
+
+### Fixed
+- After a heartbeat 404 (registry restart) the node registers again; before, it stayed unregistered.
+- Shutdown deletes every NMOS resource, the Node last, on the IS-04 paths (`/resource/nodes/{id}`); before, the DELETE went to `/resource/node/{id}`, the registry answered 404 and nothing was removed.
+- Registration failures back off (1 s doubling to 10 s).
+
 ## [1.0.1] - 2026-10-05
 
