 ## Activation
 
-An immediate IS-05 activation with `master_enable: true` writes the domain path and flow id onto the block and starts that Strom flow. `master_enable: false` stops the flow so the MXL writer or reader is destroyed. Changing the connection restarts the whole flow, including anything else in it.
+The node is the [`mxl-nmos`](https://github.com/LeeO86/mxl-nmos) crate; Strom maps its flows to the crate's resources.
+
+An IS-05 activation with `master_enable: true` writes the domain path and flow id onto the block and starts that Strom flow. `master_enable: false` stops the flow so the MXL writer or reader is destroyed. Changing the connection restarts the whole flow, including anything else in it. The activation answers once the flow has restarted, or 500 after 30 s.
+
+Activations can be immediate or scheduled (`activate_scheduled_absolute` / `activate_scheduled_relative`). Scheduled times are TAI and compared with `CLOCK_TAI`, so the host's kernel TAI offset must be set (37 s; `chronyd` with `leapsectz right/UTC` sets it). While a scheduled activation is pending, `/staged` answers 423 until the activation ran or a PATCH with `activation.mode: null` cancelled it.
 
 Senders accept `auto` for both parameters. With one visible domain, `auto` selects it. Receivers accept `auto` for the domain only, and reject `auto` for the flow id.
 
